1
00:00:01,750 --> 00:00:02,900
Two thousand years ago,

2
00:00:02,900 --> 00:00:04,850
Chinese medicine got its
founding text.

3
00:00:04,850 --> 00:00:05,850
It opens on a boast,

4
00:00:05,850 --> 00:00:08,250
and the emperor himself is
the one who makes it.

5
00:00:11,700 --> 00:00:13,676
I have heard that the
people of high antiquity,

6
00:00:13,676 --> 00:00:15,610
every one of them, lived
past a hundred years.

7
00:00:15,610 --> 00:00:16,913
Their movements never
weakened.

8
00:00:16,913 --> 00:00:18,300
The years did not wear
them down.

9
00:00:23,700 --> 00:00:26,300
It's false. Not exaggerated
— false.

10
00:00:31,400 --> 00:00:34,013
They did not. Those who
wrote it down died young,

11
00:00:34,013 --> 00:00:36,147
younger than the ancestors
they praised.

12
00:00:36,147 --> 00:00:37,640
The golden age was a
memory.

13
00:00:37,640 --> 00:00:38,600
It never happened.

14
00:00:42,050 --> 00:00:43,909
Then I have opened my
own canon with a rumour.

15
00:00:43,909 --> 00:00:45,929
The first line of the book
my physicians swear by,

16
00:00:45,929 --> 00:00:47,950
and it is only something
that somebody once heard.

17
00:00:51,800 --> 00:00:53,670
It is not lying to you. It is
persuading you.

18
00:00:53,670 --> 00:00:54,917
Those are not the same
thing —

19
00:00:54,917 --> 00:00:56,787
and the physician's
answer is narrower still:

20
00:00:56,787 --> 00:00:58,200
those among them who
knew the Way.

21
00:01:01,450 --> 00:01:03,778
So why did everyone copy
it, faithfully,

22
00:01:03,778 --> 00:01:05,116
for two thousand years?

23
00:01:05,116 --> 00:01:07,444
The Emperor's Inner
Canon. Chapter One —

24
00:01:07,444 --> 00:01:08,550
The First Sentence.

25
00:01:12,500 --> 00:01:15,877
A dramatized adaptation of
a classical philosophical

26
00:01:15,877 --> 00:01:17,500
text. Not medical advice.
